<p class="event-desc">
  On April 14, 2025, the Kaundal Artificial Intelligence & Advanced Bioinformatics Lab (KAABiL) proudly participated in the annual Plants, Soils, and Climate (PSC) Department Showcase at Utah State University. Held at the Eccles Conference Center, the showcase provided an excellent platform for our graduate students, undergraduate researchers, and interns to present their latest computational biology and bioinformatics research.
</p>
<p class="event-desc">
  During the student poster session, our team members shared innovative methodologies and findings, engaging with faculty and peers across the PSC department. The event also featured an insightful keynote address by USU alumnus Dr. Mark Slavens, followed by a departmental awards presentation. We are incredibly proud of our researchers for their hard work and dedication in representing KAABiL's ongoing contributions to plant science and computational research.
</p>
